@startuml 12-guarded-patient-deactivation
title FD-03 - Guarded Patient Deactivation
caption PAT-004/005 and section 07 private protocol; implementation pending
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Administrator as admin
participant "patients-service" as patients
participant "appointments-service" as appointments
database "appointments schema" as aptdb
database "patients schema" as patdb

admin -> patients : POST /api/v1/patients/{id}/deactivations
note right of admin
  Audited reason, expectedVersion,
  Idempotency-Key; authenticated through Gateway
end note
patients -> patients : Authorize Administrator;\nvalidate reason, version and active state
patients -> appointments : Acquire deactivation guard
appointments -> aptdb : Lock per-patient gate; check authoritative\nnon-terminal appointments and open activity guards

alt blocking appointment or activity guard
  aptdb --> appointments : Conflict
  appointments --> patients : 409 Conflict
  patients --> admin : 409; patient remains ACTIVE
else authoritative check unavailable
  appointments --> patients : Unavailable / unknown result
  patients --> admin : 503; do not deactivate
else no blockers; guard durably acquired
  appointments -> aptdb : Persist guard; block new scheduling,\nstart-of-care and conflicting activity guards
  appointments --> patients : Guard proof and operation ID
  patients -> patdb : Local transaction: compare expectedVersion;\nset INACTIVE + audit + saved result\n+ PatientDeactivated outbox
  alt patient transaction committed
    patdb --> patients : Committed
    patients -> appointments : Resolve guard as committed
    appointments -> aptdb : Finalize gate as inactive
    patients --> admin : 200 with inactive patient
  else patient transaction rejected or outcome unknown
    patients -> patients : Reconcile durable patient operation outcome
    note over patients,aptdb
      Never infer rollback from a timeout.
    end note
  end
end

note over patients,aptdb
  Reconciliation rules:
  confirmed INACTIVE -> finalize inactive gate;
  confirmed aborted before commit -> release guard;
  unknown/unavailable -> retain block and retry.
  PatientDeactivated is also an idempotent reconciliation signal.
end note

note over patients,patdb
  No automatic appointment cancellation or physical deletion.
  Inactive patients retain authorized administrative,
  clinical and financial historical access.
end note
@enduml
